Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.64,0:00:09.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to Hot Chips 2026 keynote
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.15,0:00:10.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,compute in motion
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.48,0:00:11.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,challenges of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.52,0:00:21.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,autonomous
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.90,0:00:30.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,driving.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.40,0:00:31.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.25,0:00:37.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also welcome to I personally been thinking about it as Waymo day, but it's I guess the Waymo section of Hot Chips this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.02,0:00:43.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This day has been a long time coming for Alphabet where I work and my friends at Waymo,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.60,0:00:47.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, two of whom you'll get to hear in the next couple of hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.12,0:00:50.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, by way of post lunch, everybody's falling asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.08,0:00:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Raise your hand if you've heard of Waymo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.44,0:00:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Keep your hand up if you've ridden in a Waymo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.28,0:00:56.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.71,0:00:59.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some people put their hands up and had Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.40,0:01:04.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anyway, uh, and and keep your hand up still if you've reached stage three of the Waymo experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.82,0:01:07.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Stage one is, "Oh my god, there's no driver in the car."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.59,0:01:09.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Stage two is Wow, that seems to be working.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.76,0:01:10.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a little display there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.90,0:01:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Stage three is I'm on my phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.56,0:01:15.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.18,0:01:21.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, as you'll see today, our friends at Waymo have been doing some amazing engineering.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.38,0:01:25.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I remember first hearing about it and seeing the demos and thinking, "That is so cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.66,0:01:27.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,My daughters will never have to learn how to drive."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.71,0:01:30.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I was a little over optimistic about that,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.45,0:01:37.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I think a key thing you'll see in the presentation today is incredible persistence about excellent
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.22,0:01:44.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,engineering and understanding failure cases out to I guess one of the earlier speakers today had nine nines.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.24,0:01:50.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think a bunch of the persistence that is emblematic of how my colleagues approach the incredible
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.22,0:01:58.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,safety job they do and the possibility of superhuman driving is that they have to make it work.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.52,0:02:03.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it requires incredible discipline, focus across years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.19,0:02:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It may have taken a little bit longer than my initial estimate that my now 20-year-old would never have to learn how to drive.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.64,0:02:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And yet, if you've ridden in a Waymo, it's kind of in in immediately miraculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.68,0:02:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then soon after that you realize, wow, this thing is better than I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.52,0:02:19.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like literally better than I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.21,0:02:21.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It helps that it sees in all directions, which I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.00,0:02:24.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the technology is fantastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.64,0:02:28.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the kind of thing where this is a good kind of superhum, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.80,0:02:30.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,We talk about the AI revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.33,0:02:36.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's certainly in the air and one of the reasons why many people came to the conference this year, but there are great things going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.22,0:02:42.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if we can save some fraction of the 40,000 lives a year that are lost here in America to better driving,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.14,0:02:49.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,if we can reduce property damage, if cars can just be a thing that works for us, then how much better are our lives be?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.90,0:02:55.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, by way of introduction, our keynote speaker for the conference is Daniel Rosenband.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.34,0:02:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,He and I joined Google around the same time and have known each other for most of our
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.16,0:03:04.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,time at Google because back at the time there was kind of a secretive hardware community inside of Google.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.23,0:03:08.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think when we first started working, Google wasn't out about doing hardware projects.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.27,0:03:09.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's uh been super cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.84,0:03:17.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Daniel actually spoke at Hot Chips nine years ago uh in a similar keynote, but there's way more to talk about uh today.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.20,0:03:20.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can see his bio in the uh Slack channel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.43,0:03:29.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,He has founded startups and designed DRAMs and spent the last 13 years at Waymo making their compute be what it needs to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.55,0:03:32.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I was going to say something about the the depth of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.69,0:03:33.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.37,0:03:38.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And from my personal perspective, Daniel is the constant person at Waymo,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.29,0:03:43.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the person who as long as I've been here has been the person I could call up and say, "Hey, heard about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.08,0:03:45.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is there some interesting thing we should talk about there,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.46,0:03:51.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's been super cool to have somebody with that degree of stability and persistence during the last few years.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.59,0:03:55.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'm really psyched about his talk today and I hope you enjoy it as much as we do."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.74,0:03:57.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Daniel, please take it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.44,0:04:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Cliff.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.08,0:04:05.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really good to be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.77,0:04:15.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's been a long journey at Waymo with really amazing progress and of course a lot lot is a lot of that is due to progress on the silicon side.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.69,0:04:25.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um now when we think about silicon these days of course it is all about AI right its power systems its interconnects its compute its
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.69,0:04:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,memory system right everything funnels into AI when you think about where does that AI live of course most of it today is in the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.16,0:04:42.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,data centers right enormous buildings gigawatts of power but increasingly also right
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.07,0:04:47.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have these cars driving around physical AI physical systems that very very
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.96,0:04:57.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,much rely on AI and within these physical systems of course we also have a tremendous amount of compute and semiconductors to make that possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.31,0:05:01.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So hopefully today you'll see a little bit of our journey as a company
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.31,0:05:06.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,and how important the silicon aspects are to enable compute and our autonomous drives.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.98,0:05:11.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um as part of that hopefully you also see a little bit of contrast between
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.59,0:05:20.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,what happens in the digital pure digital world and physical world in terms of AI systems.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.08,0:05:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now when we when we think about kind of physical AI few things are are clearly different right one is
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.60,0:05:34.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,just a physical scale right we want to run the biggest models we can on the car but we only
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.64,0:05:41.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,have sort of a car's worth of compute for us that's a pizza box um we we also care very
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.91,0:05:50.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,much about latency right we we have a real-time system when you're talking to your to your favorite chat AI Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.10,0:05:55.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sometimes it takes seconds, sometimes it takes minutes to respond in a physical AI system.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.47,0:05:56.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's not possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.81,0:05:57.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.21,0:06:03.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have real time latency constraints usually in the millisecond range and we need to solve for those.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.39,0:06:09.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the third aspect that's really fundamentally different is a cost of errors, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.57,0:06:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are big systems moving around.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.24,0:06:14.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could be robots, could be cars, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.03,0:06:18.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they need to behave well in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.56,0:06:21.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and maybe just one simple anecdote, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.92,0:06:26.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, uh, was recently on vacation with my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.74,0:06:28.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were creating a horse game.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.56,0:06:32.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,A horse had two legs and was jumping backwards over its jump.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.78,0:06:40.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and that's that's still pretty good and impressive for AI, but those types of things in a physical system, right, are not quite acceptable.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.73,0:06:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And she's the biggest critique, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.92,0:06:48.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,when she's in a Waymo car, she'll she'll definitely notice when we stutter for a quarter second at an intersection,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.92,0:06:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,but that's sort of a level of of sort of what of a quality bar we need to read.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.32,0:07:04.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, of course, there's also the really important aspect of of what impact are we having with the the the self-driving cars,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.07,0:07:08.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,and there one of the biggest ones, of course, is is just the safety.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.41,0:07:18.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you when you look at cars in general across the world, about one person dies every 26 seconds, right, due to a car accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.56,0:07:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so being engineers, being a company that's able to transform the world to help in those cases is of course a really awesome win.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.08,0:07:32.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So quick outline for the talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.94,0:07:37.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I'll give you a quick overview of where we've been within Waymo, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.10,0:07:44.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,what our journey has been, give a a sense of how our sensor suite has evolved and then dive into compute,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.09,0:07:51.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,finishing with what our ML models look like and what is really motivating all that compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.76,0:07:59.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So first a look back right we started Waymo in about 2009 um 10 years ago gave a talk
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.86,0:08:06.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,and was looking at some of those slides and you'll see there's sort of a the challenge picture to the
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.30,0:08:12.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,left right at the time this was a really really difficult scene for us to to support right you can
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.27,0:08:19.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,see there's a traffic light that's clearly green there's another traffic light that's occluded by a red red object Um,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.00,0:08:27.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,and sort of having the contextual information, making that really, really longtail decision, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.20,0:08:30.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you call this light red or do you call it green?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.67,0:08:32.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is not an easy thing, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.92,0:08:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's an example where it's easy to be right 90% 99% of the time, but traffic lights, you really want to be right all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.24,0:08:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, at the time, this was a really hard problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.52,0:08:52.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, today I I I I punched this into into Gemini, one of our flash models, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.24,0:08:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Query that is is a traffic light red or green and it can immediately tell you, right, what's happening in this scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.00,0:09:10.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So sort of AI has definitely advanced a long way and and helps tremendously in our journey to to have a really robust system.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.48,0:09:14.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,From a compute perspective, things have changed a lot too, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.16,0:09:21.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the time we were just transitioning from surface streets to uh sorry from freeway driving to surface streets.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.31,0:09:25.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,We knew the amount of compute would increase dramatically with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.23,0:09:25.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.60,0:09:30.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like surface streets you have more agents you you more people you interact with.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.27,0:09:33.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,The traffic rules tend to be more complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.70,0:09:37.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so we were projecting a big bump in compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.18,0:09:39.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um a fair amount of that was CPU right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.85,0:09:44.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were doing a lot of planning decisions on CPU at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.08,0:09:47.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was also our first big bump on the ML side, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.61,0:09:52.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where GPUs and other technologies started really advancing and being amazing at ML.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.04,0:09:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we we saw a nice uptick.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.68,0:09:58.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now you also see the picture on the left, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.94,0:10:01.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,This was our inspiration at the time, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.41,0:10:04.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Kind of thinking 50 TOPS, 100 TOPS.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.14,0:10:05.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow, that's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.84,0:10:08.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the world has of course changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.57,0:10:12.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and we we have a lot more TOPS now and we use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.86,0:10:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so is is good.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.04,0:10:22.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,In terms of vehicles, um we are now on our sixth generation platform.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.06,0:10:27.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our compute often iterates a little bit more quickly than these vehicle platforms.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.44,0:10:30.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but you can see a gradual transition, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.42,0:10:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We started initially with basically all off-the-shelf components.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.36,0:10:38.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Second generation started integrating sensors.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.82,0:10:47.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Third generations all all Waymo hardware and so has evolved and with closer and closer relationships with the OEMs as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.96,0:10:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're now with a sixth generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.48,0:10:52.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have an Ojai vehicle, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.74,0:10:57.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very carefully designed to be a really awesome self-driving vehicle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.12,0:10:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Also a Hyundai Ioniq 5.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.80,0:11:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a close partnership to to launch that soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.52,0:11:10.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, when you think about the trajectory of what were the capabilities of a Waymo driver,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.94,0:11:16.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,right, this is a video from 2009 and maps that we actually drove, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.80,0:11:23.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,These were kind of 10 times 100 mile challenge routes, right, that Google founders gave us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.25,0:11:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the goal was to drive these routes with zero disengages.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.24,0:11:33.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as you can see from the maps or the videos, these are actually pretty complicated routes, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.74,0:11:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Traffic lights, lane changes, pedestrians, bicyclists, toll booths, bridges, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.48,0:11:41.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,All kinds of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.75,0:11:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And within about 18 months, we we had this working, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.72,0:11:49.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which of course gave us tremendous confidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.06,0:11:51.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey, we can build self-driving cars.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.60,0:11:54.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it's really a demo, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.47,0:11:56.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,A very capable demo.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.52,0:12:02.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but it is not fully self-driving right we still had a safety driver in the driver's seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.49,0:12:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now technology-wise you can think right this is a time when we were using boosted decision trees random
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.64,0:12:17.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,forests right CNNs um transformers world models right these things didn't exist yet right so this is all based
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.43,0:12:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,on sort of pre pre new ML um technologies so where are we today right like 2009ish we we
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.08,0:12:37.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,completed those demos um it took us a good amount of time to get to fully driverless from there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.79,0:12:41.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and then even more time to really deploy at scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.50,0:12:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can see where we are today.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.20,0:12:48.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've driven over 200 million miles fully autonomously, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.31,0:12:52.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are these are rides that users use the app and take.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.04,0:12:56.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, we we are operating in 15 cities.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.26,0:12:59.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just to think about the growth curve here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.03,0:13:05.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our first 100 million miles took about 15 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.09,0:13:08.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um our second 100 million miles took about 7 months.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.88,0:13:14.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um cities right from the time we did our first fully autonomous
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.88,0:13:22.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,driving mile um until we were in four cities took about eight years.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.54,0:13:26.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just a few months ago, we launched in four cities in a single day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.67,0:13:27.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.08,0:13:32.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're at this inflection point where the technology has really matured.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.58,0:13:38.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, it works as fully autonomous technology and we're able to deploy at scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.04,0:13:41.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what's one of the things to think about here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.64,0:13:44.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like when you when you think about physical AI, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.00,0:13:47.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it often is fairly easy.
