Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.44,0:56:18.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh c can you explain how the microphone is using what are you using that for kind of wave hey Waymo and wave you down?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.71,0:56:26.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um or also do you are you permanently committed to both lidar and radar?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:26.56,0:56:26.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.00,0:56:30.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so microphone primary use is sirens, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.79,0:56:39.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,emergency vehicles and we we are able to use them both to hear and in some cases localize um honking and other nearby
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.85,0:56:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,behavior can also be important but for primary use cases as sort of emergency vehicles and then lidar and radar we're all in permanently.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.84,0:56:53.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.12,0:56:53.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.94,0:56:56.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go stage left.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.08,0:56:57.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey, thanks for the great presentation.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:57.44,0:56:59.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So my question is a little bit towards the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.04,0:57:06.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um how could you comment on trying to solve the accident problem or just driving as a coordination problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:06.32,0:57:12.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you have this one car which has a lot of sensing a lot of technology a lot of learning as a platform.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:12.36,0:57:20.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could multiple of these cars communicate or come together with an arrangement so that accidents become less likely become less ingenuous and so
Dialogue: 0,0:57:20.62,0:57:26.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,on and do could you have any comments on that and how would that change the platform the car as a computer for example?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.53,0:57:31.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, really interesting question and something we we continuously look at, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.17,0:57:33.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sort of falls under V2X technology, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:33.82,0:57:35.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can vehicles talk to vehicles?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:35.43,0:57:37.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can vehicles talk to infrastructure?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:37.70,0:57:42.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Even vehicles possibly to a cell phone in your in your pocket.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:42.42,0:57:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so we we we think some of that could be good technology, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.32,0:57:52.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it has to be deployed at scale to make a meaningful difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.12,0:57:55.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's not something we rely on as a company, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.15,0:58:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,But as adoption increases, I'm sure we'll participate in in a good way too.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.48,0:58:00.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.80,0:58:01.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:01.13,0:58:04.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,But today, right, like we we want self-driving technology today, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.88,0:58:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,V2X infrastructure doesn't exist yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:07.36,0:58:10.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so today we operate without it.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.40,0:58:10.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.86,0:58:13.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm So from Qualcomm, by the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.28,0:58:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:14.56,0:58:15.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.18,0:58:16.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Stage rate, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.72,0:58:22.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Michael Ari, NASA. Fantastic statistics compared to the average driver.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.13,0:58:29.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,How's it compare to the best and most adaptive human drivers both quantitatively if you have that
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.41,0:58:38.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,and qualitatively and then finally how can we adapt to real extreme environments like the lunar surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:38.88,0:58:41.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um first question I actually don't know the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:41.75,0:58:46.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so I think Bear, we're we're actually very transparent in our safety reports, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.68,0:58:54.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I honestly don't know if if we have a stats on the safety reports, but if you're curious, like take a look and if not, reach out, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.43,0:59:00.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Happy to connect with with people on the safety team on Lunar Surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.92,0:59:04.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, sounds really cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.11,0:59:05.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:05.84,0:59:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:06.80,0:59:10.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Stage left.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.56,0:59:11.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi, Leonard Lee.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.80,0:59:12.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Next curve.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:12.68,0:59:14.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, a really complex question here.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:14.82,0:59:19.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you mentioned GPU, but why not TPU or custom ASIC?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:19.36,0:59:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:21.28,0:59:21.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:21.58,0:59:28.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think on custom ASIC, right, I think you probably got a glimmer that yes, we are building custom silicon, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:28.05,0:59:29.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,I gave a lidar example.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:29.21,0:59:31.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I gave a sensor processing chip, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:31.11,0:59:35.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So those are custom chips we've designed within within the team.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:35.30,0:59:41.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,um they are on our cars and in some cases we've had several generations before that and they they tend
Dialogue: 0,0:59:41.93,0:59:49.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,to complement right kind of off a shelf or semi-custom solutions we we get from partners um TPUs right like of
Dialogue: 0,0:59:50.00,0:59:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,course we are we are part of Alphabet we've worked very long closely with cliff for a long time from sea
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.60,1:00:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,star days um so there's there's there's good history and good collaboration um but especially today When you look at TPU,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.16,1:00:09.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,right, like it's it's a data center chip, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:09.07,1:00:12.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,You look at edge TPU, it's a cell phone chip, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:12.45,1:00:16.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And where we are with cars is is really in between, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:16.46,1:00:25.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has different different ML requirements, uh has different environmental requirements and also sizing requirements that are somewhere in between.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:25.40,1:00:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So definitely deep collaborations.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:28.00,1:00:32.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but as with many things, it's not a one-size-fits-all.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:33.04,1:00:34.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:34.40,1:00:36.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think maybe one or two questions which is about the line.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:36.90,1:00:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So stage right please if you can go quick that'd be great.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:39.28,1:00:42.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi there it's Bruno Ben from Grabbc.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.31,1:00:47.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Daniel you talked about the interest in running very large trillion parameter models.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:47.69,1:00:53.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,U most of the time power and latency requirements preclude that.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:53.15,1:00:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but I was interested about how often would that be helpful that you can trade off in latency and compute.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:58.88,1:01:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for example,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:00.12,1:01:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,the car is slow or stationary interacting with a police officer and it might choose to switch to a very different model but still run locally.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:08.96,1:01:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.32,1:01:10.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.63,1:01:14.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's a balance we're working through, right, with these models, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.20,1:01:16.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mentioned sort of think fast, think slow, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:16.88,1:01:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So those those are increasingly modes we operate in.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:20.24,1:01:27.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so exactly what is the threshold for think slow depends on the scene and the problem you're trying to solve.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:27.76,1:01:29.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you. stage left.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:29.89,1:01:30.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Last question.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:30.95,1:01:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:31.52,1:01:35.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alexander Kaza, uh, undergrad at the University of Toronto.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:35.43,1:01:42.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering what challenges did you expect would be easy to solve that turned out to be far more difficult than you thought?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:42.23,1:01:44.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:44.08,1:01:46.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's a hard one.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:46.32,1:01:52.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I think one challenge is always the the hardware-software co-design, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:52.44,1:02:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,like we we we have an advantage of being sort of very open and and sort of small teams, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:00.12,1:02:02.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there there's no real friction.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:02.64,1:02:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the same time, everyone is running really fast, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.16,1:02:07.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're solving hard problems.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:07.90,1:02:10.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want to advance the Waymo driver.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:10.54,1:02:16.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so making sure that the teams are really working to close working together closely and and doing
Dialogue: 0,1:02:16.64,1:02:23.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,as much co-design as we could um is is sometimes more challenging than maybe expected but I think overall
Dialogue: 0,1:02:23.89,1:02:29.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,we've gotten tremendous results there and some of this is sort of self-feeding as well right based on
Dialogue: 0,1:02:29.45,1:02:35.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,the results we've achieved in the last years right expect more and more of that in the next years.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:35.52,1:02:37.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:37.36,1:02:43.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll throw in one more ideally humorous question which is I think a bunch of what you're doing
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.12,1:02:48.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,is reaching scale and the scale and miles driven and things experienced has a long tail to it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.69,1:02:53.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what was the weirdest thing a car has actually experienced that you have seen so far
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.98,1:03:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,that you can tell us about uh uh as part of this 13-year voyage in figuring out autonomy?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:04.16,1:03:11.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I guess the one slide I showed like I find the tree falling one pretty pretty unique, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:11.11,1:03:17.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I don't know of all the scenarios I thought of at least I never thought of kind of a tree falling right in front of a car.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:17.60,1:03:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not on your bingo card.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.12,1:03:19.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.46,1:03:25.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I don't know like we've seen power lines go down and other stuff like it's every time you hear these
Dialogue: 0,1:03:25.45,1:03:31.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's like oh yeah that could happen but I don't know it's hard to predict and so so there of course
Dialogue: 0,1:03:31.50,1:03:36.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,like we want to know the scenarios but we also want a model that can reason right so you don't have
Dialogue: 0,1:03:36.58,1:03:44.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,to pre-program essentially or train against every scenario but you really have that world model that can reason about what's happening.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.05,1:03:51.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I really look forward to my superhuman car noticing a situation and doing just the right thing in ways that I would have never guessed.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:51.76,1:03:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, please keep up the good work.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:53.76,1:03:59.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody, let's thank Daniel once again for a wonderful keynote.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.34,1:04:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:01.12,1:04:04.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
